From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: k230: the day field is five bits, not four

The K230 RTC DATE register holds the day of month in bits 4:0, but
k230_rtc_read_time() masks it with 0xf. Every day from the 16th to the
31st reads back sixteen days early: the 31st becomes the 15th, the 20th
becomes the 4th. k230_rtc_set_time() writes tm_mday unmasked, so a
value above 31 spills into the month field at bit 8.

The K230 SPL writes the day with the same five-bit width when it
programs the RTC for the PLL0 sleep and wake sequence.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-k230.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-k230.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-k230.c
index 4f05d2b6e..91db8685f 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-k230.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-k230.c
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ static int k230_rtc_set_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 	value = (century << DATE_YEAR_H_OFFSET) |
 		(year << DATE_YEAR_L_OFFSET) |
 		((tm->tm_mon + 1) << DATE_MONTH_OFFSET) |
-		((tm->tm_mday) << DATE_DAY_OFFSET);
+		((tm->tm_mday & 0x1f) << DATE_DAY_OFFSET);
 	rtc_writel(rtc, RTC_DATE, value);
 	value = ((tm->tm_wday) << TIME_WEEK_OFFSET) |
 		((tm->tm_hour) << TIME_HOUR_OFFSET) |
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ static int k230_rtc_read_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 	tm->tm_hour = (time_value >> TIME_HOUR_OFFSET) & 0x1f;
 	tm->tm_wday = (time_value >> TIME_WEEK_OFFSET) & 0x7;
 	tm->tm_mon  = ((date_value >> DATE_MONTH_OFFSET) & 0xf) - 1;
-	tm->tm_mday = (date_value >> DATE_DAY_OFFSET) & 0xf;
+	tm->tm_mday = (date_value >> DATE_DAY_OFFSET) & 0x1f;
 	century = (date_value >> DATE_YEAR_H_OFFSET) & 0x7f;
 	year = (date_value >> DATE_YEAR_L_OFFSET) & 0x7f;
 	tm->tm_year = century * 100 + year;
-- 
2.43.0

